        <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:selichot/penitential_third_day/haenosh_meeloah">
          <tei:pb n="119" ed="1912" facs="https://archive.org/download/selichothdavidasher1912/page/n240_medium.jpg"/>
          <tei:p>Shall mortal man be more just than God? Shall a man be more pure than his Maker? Seek ye the Lord, while he may be found, call ye upon him, while he is near. O Israel, return unto the Lord thy God, for thou hast fallen by thine iniquity. Turn ye, turn ye, thou hast said unto us, and from the beginning thou hast assured us of the value of repentance. </tei:p>
        </tei:div>
